Configure Response Interception:

   1. Navigate to Proxy -> Proxy settings -> Tools -> Proxy.
   2. Scroll to Intercept responses based on the following rules.
   3. Click Add -> Set Match type to Request -> Set Match condition to Is login request or leave it broad to look at all requests.
   4. Check the box Enabled next to the rule.
   5. Action: When you log in with bad credentials, the server's reply will freeze in Burp. Click Action -> Intercept response to this request, then manually alter the text {"success":false} to {"success":true} and click Forward.

Configure Comparer:

   1. Go to Proxy -> HTTP history.
   2. Select the valid login request, right-click, and select Send to Comparer.
   3. Select an invalid or second account login request, right-click, and select Send to Comparer.
   4. Move to the Comparer tab. Select both requests and click Words to compare parameter variations.

